  "narrative": "Synthesis for H4 validation and a necessary sign-convention reassessment for the NFE2L2/KEAP1 pair. H4 EGFR amplification versus wild type on EGFR dependency: discovery R4 is signed +0.0252 under direction -1, meaning the raw exposed-minus-comparator difference is about -0.0252, i.e. EGFR-amplified cells were slightly more dependent, but the 95% Welch interval includes zero. Independent validation R13 is signed -0.0224, meaning the raw difference is about +0.0224, the opposite direction, and the stricter independent validation interval also includes zero. The two estimates are directionally inconsistent and the combined evidence does not support a clinically meaningful expected stronger EGFR dependency, so H4 is rejected and closed. I also reassessed H8/H17 because the prior narrative treated the NFE2L2 result as reversed. Under the stated sign convention, H8/R8 is signed for direction -1; the positive signed estimate +0.796 therefore corresponds to a raw KEAP1-loss minus wild-type difference of about -0.796, i.e. much stronger NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss cells. The interval is far from zero and the effect is many times larger than the 10% relative-difference benchmark for this outcome scale, so H8 should be accepted. The reversed proposal H17, which would require a raw positive +0.796 effect, has no independent support and is rejected/closed as a sign-handling artifact rather than an empirical reversal. The robust supported findings in this dataset are: MSI-high cells have stronger WRN dependency (H1), SMARCA4-loss cells have stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H2), TP53 wild-type cells have stronger USP7 dependency relative to TP53-loss cells (H9), and KEAP1-loss cells have stronger NFE2L2 dependency relative to KEAP1 wild-type cells (H8). All have signed estimates around +0.78 to +0.80, with intervals excluding zero, and are scientifically meaningful under the 10% threshold despite possible batch/library confounding and the fact that these are associations only. Negative findings include BRAF V600E association with BRAF dependency (H3), ERBB2 amplification association with ERBB2 dependency (H5), TP53 wild-type association with MDM2 dependency (H7), KEAP1-loss original stronger-NFE2L2-rejection is superseded by H8 acceptance, MYC amplification associations with KIF18A and RPL11 dependency (H10/H11), KRAS-mutant weaker RIT1 dependency (H16), and EGFR amplification association with stronger EGFR dependency (H4). These endpoints show point estimates near zero, often in the opposite direction, or well below the 10% clinical-significance benchmark. The main unresolved mechanistic claim is KRAS mutation versus wild type on KRAS dependency (H6): the discovery raw point is only about 0.014 units stronger, around 5.5% relative, but the interval extends to roughly 12-13% relative, and KRAS dependency is a highly plausible genotype-phenotype relationship. The most informative next analysis is to test the currently unrun canonical claims H12-DHX9/MYC, H13-POLR2A/MYC, H14-TMED10/EGFR, and H15-STAT3/TP53, together with the KRAS adenocarcinoma interaction H18 and the newly proposed direct KRAS-mutation mean difference within adenocarcinoma. If H6 or the adenocarcinoma-stratified KRAS analysis shows a stable effect crossing the 10% threshold, an independent validation request should be prioritized; otherwise the KRAS main-effect follow-up can be closed. These conclusions are dataset-specific associations in a lung-lineage collection and should not be interpreted as causal or necessarily generalizable beyond this population.",
